{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Only — anything devoted, etc.</b> Our Rabbis disagreed about the matter. Some say: unspecified devotion is for sacred use, and how do I fulfil ״כָל חֵרֶם בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל לְךָ יִהְיֶה״? — for priests' herem, where he specified and said 'this is herem for the priest.' And some say: unspecified herem goes to the priest (see Sifra; Arakhin 28)." "<b>It shall not be sold and shall not be redeemed.</b> Rather, it is given to the priest. According to the one who says unspecified herem goes to priests, this verse speaks of unspecified herem; and according to the one who says unspecified herem is for the Temple maintenance, this verse speaks of priests' herem — for all agree that priests' herem has no redemption until it comes to the hand of the priest, while herem of the Most High is redeemed." "<b>Any herem is holy of holies.</b> The one who says unspecified herem is for Temple maintenance brings proof from here; and the one who says unspecified herem goes to priests expounds ״כָל חֵרֶם קֹדֶשׁ קָדָשִׁים הוּא״ to teach that priests' herem takes effect upon kodshei kodashim and upon kalim, and is given to the priest — as we learned in tractate Arakhin (28a): if it was a nedavah, he gives its best." "<b>From a person.</b> For example, one who declared herem over his Canaanite slaves and maidservants."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:03.993605490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}